# Repository Workflow

[GitHub Issues](https://github.com/th3raid0r/u-forge.ai/issues) is the source of
truth for work, audit findings, and unresolved design decisions. Keep scope,
acceptance criteria, and decisions on the issue; put implementation evidence
on the linked PR. Do not create a parallel backlog or audit ledger in the
checkout (including `.plans/`). Durable implementation contracts belong in
architecture and subsystem docs.

For tracked work, start from the issue, its latest decisions, and linked PRs.
A triage or design issue is not authorization to implement. For general
verification and autonomous workflows use the global skills for the task;
the repository-specific facts are below.

| Repository label | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `agent work` | Scoped, maintainer-authorized issue eligible for the autonomous worker queue. |
| `needs local CI` | A draft PR requests local Make checks for its recorded head SHA. See [BUILD.md](../BUILD.md) for this repository's targets. |
| `ready for review` | A draft PR requests independent review; this label does not take the PR out of draft. |
| `ready for merge` | A maintainer-controlled opt-in to hosted CI on a non-draft PR, not an approval or merge authorization. |

## Hosted CI gate

[.github/workflows/ci.yml](../.github/workflows/ci.yml) ignores changes limited
to `.md` and `.mdc` files. For other changes (including `.rules`), the job needs
both a non-draft PR and the `ready for merge` label. GitHub's native **Ready for
review** transition changes the draft state; it is not the similarly named
label. New commits rerun CI while the PR is eligible. Removing the gate label
or converting the PR back to draft cancels an in-progress run.

Hosted CI runs the Make format, workspace, strict lint, and
[graph-only test gates](testing-debugging.mdc#canonical-suites). It sets
`UFORGE_SKIP_EMBEDDED_LEMONADE=1` for the whole job so earlier Cargo steps
cannot provision the runtime. Local full verification uses the owned runtime
instead.
